-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record for Okmulgee County runs from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids January to February came in under 90% of normal in 39 of 75 years. In 2025 that pair came in at 56% of normal and November to December at 52%. So far in 2026, on the middle of the grids, January to February sits at 42% and June to July at 149%. On grid 19036 the preliminary estimate for August to September 2026 is 45.0, and RMA&rsquo;s final index can differ.</p>"}
